Package: nonignorable
Title: Shadow-Variable Screens and Sharp Sensitivity Scans for Nonignorable Missing Outcomes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Michael", "Bücker", email = "michael.buecker@fh-muenster.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Two tools for an outcome that is missing not at random.
    shadow_screen() asks whether a candidate variable can serve as a shadow
    variable, reporting its relevance for the outcome and its violation of
    the exclusion restriction on a common scale, the incremental McFadden
    R-squared (Bücker, 2026, <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2610.14695>). sharp_scan()
    asks how far the answer can move without a shadow variable: it returns
    the sharp identified set under a bound on the ratio of response
    propensities between outcome values, for the rate of a binary outcome,
    for the mean of any outcome (sharp_scan_mean()) and for its distribution
    function and quantiles (sharp_scan_cdf()). Debiased estimates and
    confidence sets with cross-fitted inputs are provided for each
    (sharp_scan_ci(), sharp_scan_mean_ci()) and for the difference between
    two groups (sharp_scan_contrast(), sharp_scan_mean_contrast()). The two
    tools answer different questions under different assumptions and are not
    two halves of one procedure.
URL: https://github.com/mchlbckr/nonignorable,
    https://buecker.ms/nonignorable/
